---
import { Code, Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import ArcantryKnowledgeGraph from './ArcantryKnowledgeGraph.astro';
---

<section class="value workflow" aria-labelledby="value-title">
  <div class="value-heading">
    <p>Three commands</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="value-title">Resume work with the project's real context</h2>
      <p>
        See what exists, choose one reviewable task, and use the project's actual format. Arcantry maps the knowledge
        sources a project already uses, keeps their responsibilities distinct, and lets you inspect, validate, or plan
        one change without adopting everything at once.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ol class="workflow-steps">
    <li>
      <div>
        <h3><Icon name="magnifier" />See the current project</h3>
        <div class="workflow-command"><Code code="arcantry context" lang="sh" /></div>
        <p>Map present and missing sources, active changes, boundaries, and available tools without writing files.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div>
        <h3><Icon name="approve-check-circle" />Choose one reviewable task</h3>
        <div class="workflow-command"><Code code="arcantry next" lang="sh" /></div>
        <p>Read the first pending task, its dependencies, and the next command while unknown approval stays unknown.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div>
        <h3><Icon name="document" />Use the project's format</h3>
        <div class="workflow-command"><Code code="arcantry explain tasks" lang="sh" /></div>
        <p>Follow the project's checklist and schema instead of introducing another workflow or document shape.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="workflow-actions">
    <a class="workflow-primary" href="/getting-started/">Try it in your project <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
    <a href="/getting-started/#work-without-the-cli">Work directly from files <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
  <div class="comparison-heading">
    <p>With and without</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="comparison-title">Make project rules explicit once</h2>
      <p>Arcantry helps when project knowledge is scattered or every tool reconstructs it differently.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="comparison-table-shell">
    <table class="comparison-flow">
      <colgroup>
        <col class="comparison-area-column">
        <col>
        <col>
      </colgroup>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Area</th>
          <th class="comparison-before-heading" scope="col">Without Arcantry</th>
          <th class="comparison-after-heading" scope="col">With Arcantry</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="magnifier" />
              <h3>Discovery</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>Every tool</strong> rebuilds project context.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p><strong>One inspection</strong> returns the same source map.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="database" />
              <h3>Responsibility</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>Sources</strong> look interchangeable.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p><strong>Each source</strong> keeps one role and owner.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="puzzle" />
              <h3>Adoption</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>One workflow</strong> requires the whole framework.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p><strong>Adopt one capability</strong> or the complete model.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>04</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="code-branch" />
              <h3>Planning</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>Automation writes</strong> before review.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p>A <strong>reviewable plan</strong> separates intent from writes.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>05</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="warning" />
              <h3>Drift</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>Old decisions</strong> overwrite newer context.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p><strong>Changed inputs</strong> stop application.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            <span>06</span>
            <div>
              <Icon name="setting" />
              <h3>Automation</h3>
            </div>
          </th>
          <td class="comparison-before">
            <p><strong>Tools duplicate</strong> boundary rules.</p>
          </td>
          <td class="comparison-after">
            <div class="comparison-result">
              <Icon name="right-arrow" />
              <p>People and tools share the <strong>same model</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="comparison-note">
    If your existing workflow already keeps these boundaries explicit and checks them consistently, Arcantry may add
    little.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="journey adoption" id="quickstart" aria-labelledby="quickstart-title">
  <div class="journey-heading">
    <p>Choose a footprint</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="quickstart-title">Start with only the boundary you need</h2>
      <p>Share a project contract, keep project knowledge private, or connect only selected sources and procedures.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ol class="journey-steps">
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="star" /></span>
      <div>
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <span class="step-label">Recommended for teams and mixed workflows</span>
        <h3>Share the contract, keep context private</h3>
        <p>Track the project agreement while workstation-specific knowledge stays outside Git.</p>
        <a href="/adoption/#shared-setup">Adopt shared + private <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="padlock" /></span>
      <div>
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <span class="step-label">For personal or workstation-specific context</span>
        <h3>Keep project knowledge outside Git</h3>
        <p>Use project-aware tools while private guidance and task context remain local to the workstation.</p>
        <a href="/adoption/#private-setup">Adopt private scope <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-icon"><Icon name="puzzle" /></span>
      <div>
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <span class="step-label">For focused agent-user collaboration</span>
        <h3>Connect only what helps</h3>
        <p>Select the sources or reusable procedures this project needs without adopting the complete model.</p>
        <a href="/skills/#three-families">Explore selected capabilities <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <nav class="journey-links" aria-label="Explore Arcantry documentation">
    <a href="/getting-started/"
      ><span><strong>Getting started</strong><small>Inspect a project safely</small></span>
      <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a
    >
    <a href="/adoption/#choose-an-adoption-path"
      ><span><strong>Adoption paths</strong><small>Compare every footprint</small></span><Icon name="right-arrow" /></a
    >
    <a href="/reference/repository-contract/#roles-in-the-stack"
      ><span><strong>Knowledge stack</strong><small>Understand each source role</small></span>
      <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a
    >
    <a href="/guides/todo-txt/"
      ><span><strong>Todo queues</strong><small>Keep task changes reviewable</small></span>
      <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a
    >
    <a href="/skills/#three-families"
      ><span><strong>Skill selection</strong><small>Choose one reusable procedure</small></span>
      <Icon name="right-arrow" /></a
    >
  </nav>
</section>

<ArcantryKnowledgeGraph />
